Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:51:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1043/1265] Text profiles for readings, and a note on every
 take

- Text profiles (heresy-textprep.js): a whole text pasted into Lyrics (now up to 10,000
  characters) is made ready to read by a profile: ordered replacement rules (literal or regular
  expression, each with a note and an on/off tick), then the shape: superscript verse numbers out,
  lines going on in lower case joined, [Intro] first, [Verse] at every blank line, [Interlude]
  after a long paragraph (sections hold the pace; without them the voice speeds up). Apply and
  Undo beside the Lyrics field, as the Key beside the Title.
- The Write tab edits profiles: rules in a table (order, on/off, regex), the shape, a live preview
  with a log of what each rule did. Built in: Reading - plain, and LCV - reading, the rules of
  Viktor's VibeVoice script (cleanup, Hebrew letters for h/t/g/v sounds, the Name, soft l, stress
  carried by other letters) as an example; anyone's own are saved on Forge (presets.json).
- A note on a take: a field in the take card, saved as you type; shown on the Collection cards
  and found by its search.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
